  "arrangerNotes": "Standard verse + chorus melody as sung today (the familiar chorus is from Pierpont's 1859 reissue; both are public domain). Verified against the Folk Tune Finder ABC (2/4 with eighth notes; here written in 4/4 with each eighth as one beat). One documented difference: in that ABC, verse bar 13 ('fun it is to') is 5, 3 2 1. We use 6, 4 3 2, as in The Session's setting (thesession.org/tunes/11656, 'Ec BA') and most published versions, because it mirrors 'o'er the fields we go'. Verse low notes 5, 6, 7 (dots below), so minLayout 11 on both drums. Medium because of the low-register verse and dotted rhythms. C and D arrangements use identical degree sequences (both fit their drums).",
  "verified": true
}
